From f3b3f62fd72831f2572126492db35111da9b4702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Martins <bgcngm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:14:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] eSimSwitcher: Update vendor modem state before switching GPIO

Notify the Oplus subsystem radio of the requested eSIM state before
changing the hardware GPIO, matching the stock framework sequence.
Without this update, dodge reports an absent card with no ATR or EID.

Enable the Java subsystem interfaces and allow the switcher to access
the vendor HAL. Check interface availability and version, and log
submission failures without blocking the existing switch sequence.

Tested on dodge: the eUICC now reports an ATR and EID, reaches
APPSTATE_READY, and its subscription reaches LOADED after switching
to eSIM.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: Icc18c8571ea8ae4882fd15bcc8f1757a358632b6
---

diff --git a/interfaces/Android.bp b/interfaces/Android.bp
index 1bea676..cc808b4 100644
--- a/interfaces/Android.bp
+++ b/interfaces/Android.bp
@@ -728,7 +728,7 @@
             enabled: true,
         },
         java: {
